Landed the write-side half only: claimed-at clamps a foreign forward-dated timestamp at our bridges, and verify notes future-dated events already in a log. The kernel-semantics half is NOT addressed and is tracked separately — evolve still evaluates each fold step at that event's own claimed :at, so an event postdated by a hostile or badly-synced replica still reaches a sticky time-gated stage permanently, and clamping OUR writes does nothing about a log that arrives already poisoned.